Cached geosite sets that explain asks through sing-box (#s96). The router
checks them after the hand lists and before it resolves a name, in render
order: the escape lane's (apple, github), then the block lane's, then the ad
set. The sandbox sing-box answers `rule-set match` from env/match-geosite-<set>,
the names that set lists:
  - github lists registry.pkg.example, so explain names the escape lane and
    the set, and does no lookup;
  - the ad set lists tracker.pixel.example, so that goes to block;
  - apple is cached but ships no answer, so it takes the "sing-box could not
    read it" path. A name no set lists reports it in a note; so does a hit
    (both hits here), since apple comes first and might have taken the name;
  - nocache is named on the escape lane with no .srs, so the router skips it,
    and a name no set lists gets a note saying so.
The .srs files are placeholders: only the stub reads them, and only to check
that they exist.
